# Git commits

- Commit every change (no matter how small) unless the user says not to.
- Write commit messages like a human: short, clear, no filler or AI-style phrasing.
- Never add Co-authored-by or any co-author trailer to commits. Do not use `--trailer "Co-authored-by: ..."` or any variant (e.g. `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`). Use plain commits only: `git commit -m "your message"` with no co-author trailers.
